<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42267" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">săgittĭfer</span></b> ,
			fĕra, fĕrum, adj.
		sagittafero. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Arrow-bearing</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pharetra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 468</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Stat. Achill. 1, 416</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Parthi,</span>”
				<i>armed with arrows</i>, <i>archers</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					11, 6</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Geloni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 725</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecus,</span>”
				i.e. <i>the porcupine</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Hystr. 48</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> =
			Sagittarius, <i>the constellation of the Archer</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Manil. 2, 266</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2,
			500</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 560</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
